{"adjusted_val_bpb": -2.6344368792870987, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No sign of getting around the measurement. The diff reads no files, uses no network, has no hard-coded coordinates, and takes all its randomness from rng, which is seeded.", "No bug that would make the result meaningless. The swap kick only runs when two radii differ by more than 0.02. Because of that guard, the set for i is never empty, and the set for j is never empty for that i. The kick swaps the two centres, shrinks both radii to the smaller one, and re-optimises through _solve_once. The repair step that comes later in the incumbent still makes the packing valid.", "Recomputed z, taking positive to mean the candidate is better: (-2.6349 - (-2.6344)) / (0.0023 * sqrt(1/1 + 1/2)) = -0.0005 / 0.00282 \u2248 -0.18 from the rounded numbers. The harness gives -0.150, which is consistent: the shown values are rounded to 4 decimals, so the real difference could be anywhere from about 0.0004 to 0.0006.", "There is only one candidate run, and the difference is far inside the noise. The candidate is not shown to be better, so the provisional reject is reasonable."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Adds a swap kick used with probability 0.4 in place of the disc kick: it exchanges the centres of two circles whose radii differ by more than 0.02, sets both radii to the smaller one, and re-optimises from that start.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "walnut", "idea_id": "b030", "incumbent_after": {"mean": -2.6348559370198386, "n": 2}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": -2.6348559370198386, "n": 2}, "job_id": "B1_p26_HH_1_s1-candidate-11_1795047671496", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.00233913, "cost_usd_plan": 0.00233913, "latency_s": 8.989920219988562, "requested_model": "haiku", "role": "coder", "served_model": "haiku", "tokens_in": 7375, "tokens_out": 2201}, {